##Authority=VCFv4.3.tex line 121 (quoted above); see DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Missing or empty ID" section: at add time, vcf-parser warns and drops such a declaration in full, for all seven keyed types (never stored, unlike a duplicate-ID-when-present).
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1) warns "[W::bcf_hrec_check] Missing ID attribute in one or more header lines" and drops the declaration, exit 0 -- BcftoolsDependencyTest#testContigMissingIdBcftoolsWarnsAndDrops pins this live measurement; re-confirmed directly via bcftools view -h on 2026-08-16. ##contig IS part of BCF's binary dictionary encoding, so unlike ##ALT/##SAMPLE/##META (see their own sibling fixtures), bcftools itself already rejects a missing ID here too -- vcf-parser's warn-and-drop is not a divergence from bcftools for this particular type.
